"Title One. Rules Applicable to All Courts | Judicial Branch of California (https://courts.ca.gov/cms/rules/index/one)\nciteturn1218search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; California Rules of Court 2026# Title One.Rules Applicable to All Courts ...     * Rule 1.300.\n\nCalifornia Rules of Court 2026\n\n# Title One. Rules Applicable to All Courts\n\nCurrent as of July 1, 2025\n\n  * Chapter 1. Preliminary Rules\n\n    * Rule 1.1. The California Rules of Court\n    * Rule 1.2. Title\n    * Rule 1.3. Authority\n    * Rule 1.4. Contents of the rules\n    * Rule 1.5. Construction of rules and standards\n    * Rule 1.6. Definitions and use of terms\n  * Chapter 2. Timing and Holidays\n\n    * Rule 1.10. Time for actions\n    * Rule 1.11. Holiday falling on a Saturday or Sunday\n  * Chapter 3. Service and Filing\n\n    * Rule 1.20. Effective Date of Filing\n    * Rule 1.21. Service\n    * Rule 1.22. Recycled paper [Repealed]\n  * Chapter 4. Judicial Council Forms\n\n    * Rule 1.30. Judicial Council forms\n    * Rule 1.31. Mandatory forms\n    * Rule 1.35. Optional forms\n    * Rule 1.37. Use of forms\n    * Rule 1.40. Statutory references on forms\n    * Rule 1.41. Proofs of service on forms\n    * Rule 1.42. Forms not to be rejected\n    * Rule 1.43. Legibility\n    * Rule 1.44. Electronically produced forms\n    * Rule 1.45. Judicial Council pleading forms\n    * Rule 1.51. California Law Enforcement Telecommunications System (CLETS) information form\n  * Chapter 5. Accommodations\n\n    * Rule 1.100. Requests for accommodations by persons with disabilities\n  * Chapter 6. Public Access to Court Proceedings\n\n    * Rule 1.150. Photographing, recording, and broadcasting in court\n  * Chapter 7. Form and Format of Papers\n\n    * Rule 1.200. Format of citations\n    * Rule 1.201. Protection of privacy\n  * Chapter 8. Language Access Services\n\n    * Rule 1.300. Access to programs, services, and professionals\n\n### Attached Documents\n\nroc-title-1--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/the-central-guide/TCGSupp1002-1%28c%29_Checklists%20of%20Petition%20Forms.pdf)\nciteturn1218view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 27; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1212view1\",\"id\":15}); Redirected to URL: https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/the-central-guide/TCGSupp1002-1(c)_Checklists%20of%20Petition%20Forms.pdf; Total lines: 802\nL0@P0: URL: https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/the-central-guide/TCGSupp1002-1(c)_Checklists%20of%20Petition%20Forms.pdf\nL1@P0: Court Manual Supplement 1002-1(c) August 2025\nL2@P0: The Central Guide Supplement to LBR 1002-1(c)\nL3@P0: Checklists of Forms Required\nL4@P0: to File a Bankruptcy Case\nL5@P0: Voluntary Cases – Chapters 7, 11, 12, and 13\nL6@P0-1: Involuntary Cases – Chapters 7 and 11 onlyCourt Manual Supplement 1002-1(c) August 2025\nL7@P1-2: This Page Intentionally Left BlankCourt Manual Supplement 1002-1(c) August 2025\nL8@P2: Case Commencement (Bankruptcy Petition) Documents\nL9@P2: (a) General Requirements [LBR 1002-1]. The following requirements must\nL10@P2: be met in order to file a voluntary petition and other case commencement\nL11@P2: documents with the court, either electronically or non-electronically, with the\nL12@P2: exception of chapter 9 and 15. Minimum requirements for filing a chapter\nL13@P2: 7, 11, 12 or 13 bankruptcy case, and a complete list of documents required\nL14@P2: to complete the filing and their corresponding deadlines, are detailed in\nL15@P2: sections 1.1(b) through 1.1(h).\nL16@P2: (1) Deadline to File Required Documents. Unless extended by court\nL17@P2: order, the balance of the documents required by the FRBP must be\nL18@P2: filed within 14 days of the petition date, except the Statement of\nL19@P2: Intention in a chapter 7 case, which must be filed not later than 30\nL20@P2: days after the filing of the petition.\nL21@P2: (2) Debtor’s Address. If a petition is filed under 11 U.S.C. §§ 301, 302,\nL22@P2: 303, or 1504, the debtor’s actual street address must be disclosed in\nL23@P2: addition to any post office box address.\nL24@P2: (3) Attorney Information.\nL25@P2: (A) General. A voluntary petition filed pursuant to 11 U.S.C. §§\nL26@P2: 301 and 302 by an attorney on behalf of any party must\nL27@P2: contain the attorney’s state bar identification number,\nL28@P2: telephone number, fax number, and e-mail address in the\nL29@P2: attorney name block.\nL30@P2: (B) Signature of Counsel. The name of the attorney signing a\nL31@P2: petition must be printed clearly below the signature line.\nL32@P2: (4) Divisions - Place of Filing [LBR 1071-1].\nL33@P2: (A) Filing of Petition. Unless otherwise ordered by the court, a\nL34@P2: petition commencing a case under the Bankruptcy Code must\nL35@P2: be filed in the “applicable division.” The “applicable division”\nL36@P2: is determined by the location of the debtor’s residence,\nL37@P2: principal offices, officers, and books and records, or where the\nL38@P2: majority of the debtor’s assets are located based on a book\nL39@P2: value determination as set forth on the debtor’s most current\nL40@P2: balance sheet. (Refer to Appendix B for the applicable\nL41@P2-3: division.)Court Manual Supplement 1002-1(c) August 2025\nL42@P3: (B) Filing of Documents Other Than Petition Case\nL43@P3: Commencement Documents. Documents other than a\nL44@P3: petition must be filed only in the divisional office of the clerk to\nL45@P3: which the relevant cases or proceeding has been assigned.\nL46@P3: However, the clerk may, by special waiver or upon order of\nL47@P3: the court, accept documents in any office of the clerk\nL48@P3: irrespective of the division.\nL49@P3: (5) Petition Forms. Complete petition packages with instructions are\nL50@P3: available at no charge from the court’s website,\nL51@P3: <www.cacb.uscourts.gov> ->Forms -> Petition Forms.\nL52@P3: (A) Case Commencement Documents Filed Electronically. A\nL53@P3: paper copy of any case commencement document filed\nL54@P3: electronically is not required to be served on the judge or\nL55@P3: provided to the court.\nL56@P3: (b) Chapter 7 Individual (Bankruptcy Petition) Documents.\nL57@P3: (1) At a minimum, documents (A, B, and C), MUST BE FILED, when\nL58@P3: applicable, or the bankruptcy filing will not be accepted.\nL59@P3: (A) Statement About Your Social Security Numbers -- If filing\nL60@P3: electronically, this document must be filed separately\nL61@P3: from the other documents in this package.\nL62@P3: (B) Voluntary Petition for Individuals Filing for Bankruptcy (Official\nL63@P3: Form 101) -- this completed form must be signed by the\nL64@P3: debtor(s) after the debtor(s) has read the Notice Required by\nL65@P3: 11 U.S.C. § 342(b) for Individuals Filing Bankruptcy (Form\nL66@P3: 2010) that is available on the court’s website.\nL67@P3: (C) Master Mailing List of Creditors -- this is not a form; it is a list\nL68@P3: of creditors’ names and addresses. Please see the\nL69@P3: Requirements for Master Mailing List of Creditors in section\nL70@P3: 1.3 .\nL71@P3: (D) Initial Statement About an Eviction Judgment Against You\nL72@P3: (Official Form 101A) – this form must be filed with your\nL73@P3: voluntary petition IF you marked “Yes” to both questions\nL74@P3: in #11 on the Voluntary Petition for Individuals Filing for\nL75@P3: Bankruptcy (Official Form 101). As required by LBR 4001-\nL76@P3: 1, the filer must attach to this Official Form 101A: 1) a check\nL77@P3: in the form of a certified cashier’s check or money order\nL78@P3: payable to the lessor or landlord in the amount of any rent that\nL79@P3-4: would become due during the 30-day period after filing of the Court Manual Supplement 1002-1(c) August 2025\nL80@P4: bankruptcy petition; and 2) a copy of the judgment for\nL81@P4: possession (LBR 4001-1).\nL82@P4: The Following Documents Must be Filed with the Voluntary\nL83@P4: Petition or within 14 Days After Filing the Voluntary Petition\nL84@P4: The following documents, if applicable, MUST also be filed at\nL85@P4: the bankruptcy court with the Voluntary Petition, or within 14\nL86@P4: days after the filing of the Voluntary Petition. If the following\nL87@P4: documents are not filed within 14 days after the filing of the\nL88@P4: Voluntary Petition, the bankruptcy case may be dismissed. If\nL89@P4: that happens, the debtor will lose whatever filing fees were paid,\nL90@P4: and the debtor’s creditors will be able to resume collection\nL91@P4: activities.\nL92@P4: (E) Debt Repayment Plan – if the credit counseling agency\nL93@P4: provided the debtor with a debt repayment plan, the debt\nL94@P4: repayment plan must be filed.\nL95@P4: (F) Statement of Related Cases (LBR Form F1015-\nL96@P4: 2.1.STMT.RELATED.CASES).\nL97@P4: (G) Summary of Your Assets and Liabilities and Certain Statistical\nL98@P4: Information (Official Form 106Sum).\nL99@P4: (H) Schedules A/B through J-2 -- If any of the applicable\nL100@P4: schedules do not apply, the debtor MUST print “NONE” on the\nL101@P4: form and file it with the other documents.\nL102@P4: Schedule A/B: Property (Official Form 106A/B)\nL103@P4: Schedule C: The Property You Claim as Exempt (Official\nL104@P4: Form 106C)\nL105@P4: Schedule D: Creditors Who Have Claims Secured by Property\nL106@P4: (Official Form 106D)\nL107@P4: Schedule E/F: Creditors Who Have Unsecured Claims\nL108@P4: (Official Form 106E/F)\nL109@P4: Schedule G: Executory Contracts and Unexpired Leases\nL110@P4: (Official Form 106G)\nL111@P4: Schedule H: Your Codebtors (Official Form 106H)\nL112@P4-5: Schedule I: Your Income (Official Form 106I)Court Manual Supplement 1002-1(c) August 2025\nL113@P5: Schedule J: Your Expenses (Official Form 106J)\nL114@P5: Schedule J-2: Expenses for Separate Household of Debtor 2\nL115@P5: (Official Form 106J-2). You must file Official Form 106J-2 if\nL116@P5: you answered “yes” to both questions on Official Form 106J,\nL117@P5: Part 1.\nL118@P5: (I) Declaration About an Individual Debtor's Schedules (Official\nL119@P5: Form 106Dec).\nL120@P5: (J) Statement of Financial Affairs for Individuals Filing For\nL121@P5: Bankruptcy (Official Form 107).\nL122@P5: (K) Disclosure of Compensation of Bankruptcy Petition Preparer\nL123@P5: (Official Form 2800) -- this form must be filed if the debtor paid\nL124@P5: a non-attorney bankruptcy petition preparer to prepare any of\nL125@P5: the bankruptcy filing documents [11 U.S.C. § 110].\nL126@P5: (L) Bankruptcy Petition Preparer’s Notice, Declaration and\nL127@P5: Signature (Official Form 119) -- this form must be filed if the\nL128@P5: debtor paid a non-attorney bankruptcy petition preparer to\nL129@P5: prepare any of the bankruptcy filing documents [11 U.S.C. §\nL130@P5: 110].\nL131@P5: (M) Disclosure of Compensation of Attorney for Debtor (Official\nL132@P5: Form 2030) -- this form is required when an attorney\nL133@P5: represents the debtor and/or prepared the bankruptcy filing\nL134@P5: documents. This form is not required if LBR form F 2090-\nL135@P5: 1.CH7.ATTY.COMP.DISCLSR is filed.\nL136@P5: (N) Attorney’s Disclosure of Compensation Arrangement in\nL137@P5: Individual Chapter 7 Case (LBR form F 2090-\nL138@P5: 1.CH7.ATTY.COMP.DISCLSR) -- this form is filed if the\nL139@P5: debtor agreed to pay an attorney a specific amount for limited\nL140@P5: services.\nL141@P5: (O) Declaration by Debtor(s) as to Whether Income was Received\nL142@P5: From an Employer within 60 Days of the Petition Date [11\nL143@P5: U.S.C.§ 521(a)(1)(B)(iv)] (LBR form F 1002-\nL144@P5: 1.EMP.INCOME.DEC). If filing electronically, this\nL145@P5: document must be filed separately from the other\nL146@P5: documents in this package.\nL147@P5: (P) Chapter 7 Statement of Your Current Monthly Income (Official\nL148@P5-6: Form 122A-1).Court Manual Supplement 1002-1(c) August 2025\nL149@P6: (Q) Statement of Exemption from Presumption of Abuse Under §\nL150@P6: 707(b)(2) (Official Form 122A-1SUPP).\nL151@P6: (R) Chapter 7 Means Calculation (Official Form 122A-2).\nL152@P6: (S) Verification of Master Mailing List of Creditors [LBR 1007-1(a)]\nL153@P6: (LBR form F 1007-1.MASTER.MAILING.VERIFICATION).\nL154@P6: (T) Certificate of Credit Counseling - a certificate of credit\nL155@P6: counseling is issued by the credit counseling agency after the\nL156@P6: debtor has completed a credit counseling course. This\nL157@P6: document must be filed separately from the other\nL158@P6: documents in this package.\nL159@P6: The Following Document Must be Filed with the Voluntary\nL160@P6: Petition or within 30 Days After Filing the Voluntary Petition\nL161@P6: (U) Statement of Intention for Individuals Filing Under Chapter 7\nL162@P6: (Official Form 108) -- this form must be filed within 30 days\nL163@P6: from filing of the bankruptcy case or by the date set for the\nL164@P6: meeting of creditors [11 U.S.C. § 521(a)(2)(A)].\nL165@P6: (V) Statement About Payment of an Eviction Judgment Against\nL166@P6: You (Official Form 101B) – if you filed Official Form 101A (see\nL167@P6: E) - this form must be filed within 30 days after the filing of the\nL168@P6: Voluntary Petition if the Debtor(s) wishes to stay in their\nL169@P6: residence for more than 30 days after filing the Voluntary\nL170@P6: Petition.\nL171@P6: Optional Form with No Deadline for Filing\nL172@P6: (W) Debtor’s Request to Activate Electronic Noticing (DeBN)\nL173@P6: (local form F 9036-1.DeBN.ACTIVATE) -- this is an optional\nL174@P6: form for individual debtors to request orders and court\u0002generated notices by email (at no cost) through the DeBN\nL175@P6: program, instead of by U.S. mail. If filing electronically, this\nL176@P6: document must be filed separately from the other\nL177@P6-7: documents in this package.Court Manual Supplement 1002-1(c) August 2025\nL178@P7: (c) Chapter 7 Non-Individual (Bankruptcy Petition) Documents.\nL179@P7: (1) At a minimum, documents (A and B), MUST BE FILED, when\nL180@P7: applicable, or the bankruptcy filing will not be accepted.\nL181@P7: (A) Voluntary Petition for Non-Individuals Filing for Bankruptcy\nL182@P7: (Official Form 201) -- this completed form must be signed by\nL183@P7: the authorized representative of the Debtor(s).\nL184@P7: (B) Master Mailing List of Creditors – this is not a form; it is a list\nL185@P7: of creditors’ names and addresses. Please see the\nL186@P7: Requirements for Master Mailing List of Creditors in section\nL187@P7: 1.3 .\nL188@P7: The Following Documents Must be Filed with the Voluntary\nL189@P7: Petition or within 14 days After Filing the Voluntary Petition\nL190@P7: The following documents, if applicable, MUST also be filed at\nL191@P7: the bankruptcy court with the Voluntary Petition, or within 14\nL192@P7: days after the filing of the Voluntary Petition. If the following\nL193@P7: documents are not filed within 14 days after the filing of the\nL194@P7: Voluntary Petition, the bankruptcy case may be dismissed. If\nL195@P7: that happens, the debtor will lose whatever filing fees were paid,\nL196@P7: and the debtor’s creditors will be able to resume collection\nL197@P7: activities.\nL198@P7: (C) Corporate Resolution Authorizing Filing of the Petition – this\nL199@P7: is not a form and is required only if the debtor is a corporation.\nL200@P7: (D) Corporate Ownership Statement (LBR form F 1007-\nL201@P7: 4.CORP.OWNERSHIP.STMT) – this is required only if the\nL202@P7: debtor is a corporation (other than a government unit) [LBR\nL203@P7: 1007-4].\nL204@P7: (E) Statement of Related Cases (LBR form F 1015-\nL205@P7: 2.1.STMT.RELATED.CASES).\nL206@P7: (F) Summary of Assets and Liabilities for Non-Individuals (Official\nL207@P7: Form 206Sum).\nL208@P7: (G) Schedules A/B, D through H -- If any of the applicable\nL209@P7: schedules do not apply, the debtor MUST print “NONE” on the\nL210@P7: form and file it with the other documents).\nL211@P7: Schedule A/B: Assets – Real and Personal Property (Official\nL212@P7-8: Form 206A/B)Court Manual Supplement 1002-1(c) August 2025\nL213@P8: Schedule D: Creditors Who Have Claims Secured by Property\nL214@P8: (Official Form 206D)\nL215@P8: Schedule E/F: Creditors Who Have Unsecured Claims\nL216@P8: (Official Form 206E/F)\nL217@P8: Schedule G: Executory Contracts and Unexpired Leases\nL218@P8: (Official Form 206G)\nL219@P8: Schedule H: Your Codebtors (Official Form 206H)\nL220@P8: (H) Declaration Under Penalty of Perjury for Non-Individual\nL221@P8: Debtors (Official Form 202).\nL222@P8: (I) Statement of Financial Affairs for Non-Individuals Filing For\nL223@P8: Bankruptcy (Official Form 207).\nL224@P8: (J) Disclosure of Compensation of Attorney for Debtor (Official\nL225@P8: Form 2030) -- this form is required when an attorney\nL226@P8: represents the debtor and/or prepared the bankruptcy filing\nL227@P8: documents.\nL228@P8: (K) Verification of Master Mailing List of Creditors [LBR 1007-1(a)]\nL229@P8: (LBR form F 1007-1.MAILING.LIST.VERIFICATION).\nL230@P8: Optional Form with No Deadline for Filing\nL231@P8: (L) Debtor’s Request to Activate Electronic Noticing (DeBN) -\nL232@P8: local form F 9036‐1.1.DeBN.ACTIVATE) – this is an optional\nL233@P8: form for the debtor’s authorized representative to request\nL234@P8: orders and court-generated notices by email (at no cost),\nL235@P8: instead of by U.S. mail. If filing electronically, this\nL236@P8: document must be filed separately from the other\nL237@P8: documents in this package.\nL238@P8: (d) Chapter 11 Individual (Bankruptcy Petition) Documents.\nL239@P8: (1) At a minimum, documents (A, B, C, and D), MUST BE FILED,\nL240@P8: when applicable, or the bankruptcy filing will not be accepted.\nL241@P8: (A) Statement About Your Social Security Numbers (Official Form\nL242@P8: 121) -- If filing electronically, this document must be filed\nL243@P8: separately from the other documents in this package. See\nL244@P8: Court Manual, section 3.6(b).\nL245@P8: (B) Voluntary Petition for Individuals Filing for Bankruptcy (Official\nL246@P8: Form 101) -- this completed form must be signed by the\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/the-central-guide/TCGSupp1002-1%28d%29_Privacy-Policy.pdf)\nciteturn1218view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 3; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1212view1\",\"id\":16}); Redirected to URL: https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/the-central-guide/TCGSupp1002-1(d)_Privacy-Policy.pdf; Total lines: 34\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/the-central-guide/TCG-Supp-1007-1%28a%29_Master-Mailing-List.pdf)\nciteturn1218view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 4; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1212view1\",\"id\":17}); Redirected to URL: https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/the-central-guide/TCG-Supp-1007-1(a)_Master-Mailing-List.pdf; Total lines: 61\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/the-central-guide/TCGSupp1071-1%28a%29%281%29_ZipCodes-Regions.pdf)\nciteturn1218view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 6; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1212view1\",\"id\":18}); Redirected to URL: https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/the-central-guide/TCGSupp1071-1(a)(1)_ZipCodes-Regions.pdf; Total lines: 66\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/sites/cacb/files/documents/the-central-guide/TCGSupp1071-1%28a%29%282%29_Phone-Directory-Locations.pdf)\ncite